claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> Agents need to read list mail, and should keep reading while
> Fastmail is down. mbsync pulls new messages from the Fastmail folder
> lists into a local maildir once a minute. It is configured to only
> pull new messages, so nothing an agent does here can flag, move, or
> delete mail on Fastmail, and the local copy only ever grows.

We describe it as append-only - how did only ever grows get in here?

> The maildir lives outside the jail root so a rebuild does not fetch
> the folder again. mbsync creates its files readable only by itself;
> the fetch job opens them for reading so an IMAP server running as
> another user can serve them without being able to change them.
